LD_VTX_GPU_INDEX=1 (default off; only together with LD_VTX_GPU=1): indexed TRIANGLES draws on the GPU-fetch path (KZ3 patch 2076)
use the guest index buffer directly. The indices are converted to little-endian u32 as the D3D index buffer, the vertex buffer is
a fixed identity table (entry k = k, 0x100000 entries, made once) and BaseVertexLocation is the RSX base index, so the shader's
element is index + base index, as rsx_vg_element gives it; the decode block covers [min, max] + base. The per-occurrence
references (refs), the unique-vertex hash (remap) and the 4-byte element payload go away for those draws. Restart values in the
data, a 20-bit wrap, an index count that is not a multiple of 3, other primitives, array or inline batches and every refused GPU
plan keep the old path. New header libs/video/rsx_vg_index.h (pure, host-tested: R&C port/rc/tests/run_vg_index_test.sh).
R&C ToD: P1 measured refs + remap + copy ~218 ms/s of the walker. ENHANCEMENT (performance; output identical by construction).
Rebased onto v0.18.0 + KZ3 2c5081a5, 2026-11-02: same logic. Patch 7010 is dropped (KZ3 2089 does it), so the include
sits right after rsx_live_draw.h (2026-11-09: after KZ3 2156's two includes, which come first in patch order). The index write joins KZ3 2093's timed index branch as its own else-if before it; the
vertex-buffer view keeps KZ3 2092's device-cache hit first (a GPU-fetch draw never uses the vertex cache: ld_vc is off
with LD_VTX_GPU=1, so vg_direct and vd_hit never meet).

